'''Stygeon Prime''', also known simply as '''Stygeon''', was a [[mountain]]ous, [[Water|snowy]] [[planet]] located in the [[Stygeon system]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]' [[Nuiri sector]]. The world's blizzard conditions made it the perfect location for a prison, as prisoners attempting escape would not survive outside the prison walls unless they could use a local [[tibidee]] to fly them to safety. 

==Description==
Stygeon Prime, otherwise known as Stygeon, was a [[mountain]]ous and [[Water|snow]]-covered [[planet]]<ref name="Stygeon Prime" /> located in the [[Stygeon system]]<ref name="Rise of the Old Masters" /> of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]'<ref name="Head to Head" /> [[Nuiri sector]].<ref name="Epic Battles" /> The planet was 9,100 [[kilometer]]s in diameter,<ref name="FF72" /> and held a Type I [[atmosphere]], with a mixture of [[oxygen]], [[hydrogen]] and [[nitrogen]],<ref name="BMF 73" /> as well as a thin<ref name="FF72" /> and cold climate.<ref name="Stygeon Prime" /> In [[orbit]] of a single [[star]]<ref name="BMF 73" /> and orbited by two [[moon]]s,<ref name="FF72" /> Stygeon was almost completely devoid of native life,<ref name="BMF 73" /> except for the large [[tibidee]] creatures that called it home.<ref name="Stygeon Prime" /> Thanks to its conditions the world was an ideal location for a [[prison]] as [[Prisoner|escapees]] would not usually survive outside the prison walls.<ref name="VE" />

==History==
After her [[Mission to Numidian Prime|capture]]<ref name="MA">''[[Master & Apprentice]]''</ref> in around [[66 BBY]],<ref name="MA date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' places the main events of ''[[Master & Apprentice]]'' in [[40 BBY]]. The novel also establishes that [[Qui-Gon Jinn]] was forty [[Standard year|years]] old during its main events and fourteen years old in the [[Numidian Prime]] [[Mission to Numidian Prime|mission]], which dates the endeavor to around [[66 BBY]].</ref> the notorious [[bounty hunter]] and [[assassin]] [[Shenda Mol]] was put "on ice" at Stygeon Prime.<ref name="MA" /> During the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Sith Lord]]s [[Dooku|Darth Tyranus]] and [[Darth Sidious]] [[Prisoner|imprisoned]] Sidious's former [[Sith apprentice|apprentice]] [[Maul]] in the [[Spire (Stygeon Prime)|Spire]], a [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Confederate]] [[prison]] on Stygeon Prime. Maul was later [[Escape from the Spire|broken out]] by [[Mandalorian]] [[Mandalorian super commando|forces]] that were part of his [[Shadow Collective]].<ref name="Son of Dathomir 1" /> After the Clone Wars, the planet was occupied by the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Visual Guide" /> The Empire and its [[Inquisitorius]] used the Spire and imprisoned and later [[Death penalty|executed]] the [[Jedi]] [[Jedi Master|Master]] [[Luminara Unduli]] there, while her remains were kept in her former cell in order to lure out any survivors of [[Order 66]].<ref name="Rise of the Old Masters" /> In [[5 BBY]],<ref name="Rebels date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> the rebellious [[Spectres|crew]] of the ''[[Ghost]]'' learned of Unduli and [[Duel on Stygeon Prime|attempted]] to save her before only nearly escaping the [[the Grand Inquisitor]].<ref name="Rise of the Old Masters" />

{{Planet-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The planet Stygeon Prime, referred to then as Stygeon, was first mentioned in the [[Blaster (department)|''Blaster'']] segment of [[Star Wars Insider 149|''Star Wars Insider'' 149]], which discussed the upcoming [[Star Wars: Darth Maul — Son of Dathomir|''Star Wars: Darth Maul—Son of Dathomir'']] miniseries. It first appeared in the [[Darth Maul — Son of Dathomir 1|first issue]].<ref name="Son of Dathomir 1" /> The planet's full name was revealed in ''[[Star Wars Rebels: The Visual Guide]]''.<ref name="Visual Guide" />

